    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>Created by the division of Lotharingia in 959, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lorraine">Lorraine</a> was ruled from 1048 to 1737 by the descendants of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gerard-of-alsace">Gerard of Alsace</a>.</li><li><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rene-ii-duke-of-lorraine">René II</a>’s victory at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-nancy">Nancy</a> in 1477, where <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-the-bold">Charles the Bold</a> died, secured the duchy between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> and the Empire.</li><li>French occupations from 1633 and the exchange for Tuscany in 1737 ended its independence; it became French in 1766.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>The last duke, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francis-i-holy-roman-emperor">Francis Stephen</a>, married <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maria-theresa">Maria Theresa</a> and became <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holy-roman-emperor">Holy Roman Emperor</a>; their house of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-habsburg-lorraine">Habsburg-Lorraine</a> ruled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a> until 1918.</p></aside>
    </section>

